-- expect-refusal: un_p negates un_q, and neither is ranked by stratum/2
-- examples/checks/strata-unranked-negation-3-refused.rofl — under the stock
-- evaluator with no stratum table, a negation of a relation another unranked
-- rule derives. Both rules share the final pass, so p fires beside q(1) or
-- before it, by their canonical order and not by the meaning: the program
-- answered p(1) beside q(1), exit 0, and is refused.
edb(un_b).
un_b(1).
un_b(2).
un_r(2) :- un_b(2).
un_q(1) :- un_b(1), not un_r(1).
un_p(X) :- un_b(X), not un_q(X).
